WEBVTT

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.987
What?

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.993
I've seen that look before.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.551
Ensign Murphy
had better watch out.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.393
I happen to know
that Murphy is seeing

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.762
one of the Delaney sisters.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.996
Not since Harry and Tom Paris
made their move.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.664
Harry and the Delaney sisters?

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.673
He would have told me.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.972
I guess there are some things
he keeps to himself.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.204
Harry...

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:49.409
is it true about you
and the Delaney sisters?

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.746
Is what true?

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.012
Come on, Harry.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.780
There aren't any secrets
on a ship this small.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.156
What have you been
telling people?

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.457
Well, we did take that trip
to Venice with them.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.792
The holodeck?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.320
You got to be kidding.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.299
That lasted all of 15 minutes.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.631
Yeah, you know I've been
meaning to ask you.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.331
What happened
when you and Jenny Delaney

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.203
disappeared in that gondola?

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.208
Nothing.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.971
Harry, we're your friends.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.341
You can tell us.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.539
Nothing.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.445
We... talked.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.712
And then...

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.515
I fell over the side.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:31.490
You fell out of the gondola?

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.389
I think maybe Harry
wasn't quite prepared

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:37.522
for how voracious
Jenny Delaney can be.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.099
I think it's finally
beginning to happen.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.969
Both crews getting along.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.974
That kind of bonding
should improve performance

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.566
and maximize efficiency.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.010
Yes, I'm sure it will.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.014
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.174
Go ahead.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.684
Captain, we're receiving
a distress call

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.015
in one of the lower
subspace bands.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.385
I'm on my way.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.981
- This is it.
- Thanks.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.293
Report, Commander.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.628
The subspace distress signal's

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.896
coming from a vessel
bearing 125 mark 21.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.301
Distance: 200,000 kilometers.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.771
Captain...

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.865
sensors indicate
five life-forms aboard.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.309
The vessel is altering
its course to intercept us.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.142
Go to Yellow Alert
and slow to impulse.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.478
- Hail them, Mr. Kim.
- Aye, Captain.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.485
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.419
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.479
What is the nature
of your emergency?

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.514
We have no emergency.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.083
But you're sending out
a distress call.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.617
Yes, we are.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.562
Why?

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.792
Because you are in distress.

00:04:43.648 --> 00:04:46.708
I am Gathorel Labin
of the planet Sikaris.

00:04:46.751 --> 00:04:49.720
Please, let us welcome you
to our system,

00:04:49.754 --> 00:04:52.120
show you the hospitality
of our people.

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:53.454
That's very kind of you...

00:04:53.491 --> 00:04:55.516
if I could come aboard
your ship,

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.391
I have gifts for you

00:04:57.429 --> 00:05:00.660
and a proposal I hope
you will find irresistible.

00:05:04.302 --> 00:05:08.204
Mr. Tuvok, make
the necessary arrangements

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.401
to receive our guest.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.310
Ah...

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:24.615
Mr. Labin, it really
isn't necessary

00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:25.953
to go to all of this trouble.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.253
Please, call me Gath.

00:05:27.292 --> 00:05:28.919
And I promise you,
I would like nothing better

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.259
than to prepare a few of our
newest delicacies for you.

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:33.559
Ah, this will be perfect.

00:05:33.598 --> 00:05:38.365
Uh-uh, Captain, I'm serving
lunch in less than two hours.

00:05:38.403 --> 00:05:39.529
We won't be long, Neelix.

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:41.664
This is Mr...
this is Gath.

00:05:41.706 --> 00:05:42.968
He's from Sikaris.

00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:46.067
Ooh, Sikaris.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:47.772
Do you know the planet?

00:05:47.812 --> 00:05:52.306
Only stories about their
incredible hospitality.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.342
Tell me,
how do you know about us?

00:05:55.387 --> 00:05:58.356
Our people are
very well-traveled.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.483
Some of them have
brought back stories

00:06:00.525 --> 00:06:01.651
about the ship of aliens

00:06:01.693 --> 00:06:03.251
from another part
of the galaxy...

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.695
people lost and alone,

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.925
struggling to find
their way home again.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.660
This is wonderful.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.931
And I decided
to come and meet you,

00:06:12.003 --> 00:06:13.493
and offer you respite.

00:06:13.538 --> 00:06:14.505
Respite?

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:16.666
A vacation, if you will...

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:19.108
get away from the confines
of the ship,

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.442
enjoy the beauty
of our landscape,

00:06:21.479 --> 00:06:25.609
meet and talk with interesting,
learned people.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.379
And the crew
would certainly welcome

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:28.852
a little shore leave, Captain.

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.354
And I hear the Sikarians

00:06:30.388 --> 00:06:33.050
have a huge variety
of edible plants.

00:06:33.091 --> 00:06:35.252
If we could collect some seeds,

00:06:35.293 --> 00:06:38.820
we'd expand
our selection significantly.

00:06:38.863 --> 00:06:41.696
Sounds like all this
would increase performance

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:43.200
and maximize efficiency.

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:44.895
Don't you think, Mr. Tuvok?

00:06:46.471 --> 00:06:47.961
Indeed.

00:06:48.006 --> 00:06:51.464
Well, Gath, looks like
you're getting visitors.

00:06:51.509 --> 00:06:54.205
We'll set a course
and follow you in.

00:06:54.245 --> 00:06:56.270
I could not be happier.

00:07:04.322 --> 00:07:09.885
If you see anything you like,
just let me know.

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:14.932
What is this material?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.558
It's so delicate.

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:17.932
Exquisite, isn't it?

00:07:17.969 --> 00:07:20.529
It's the latest import
from Dedestris.

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:23.040
It's spun
from the petals of a flower

00:07:23.074 --> 00:07:25.065
that blooms only in moonlight.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.374
Shall I have
a dress made for you?

00:07:27.412 --> 00:07:29.937
It's lovely,
but, no... thank you.

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:33.745
Is it so hard
for you to accept a gift?

00:07:33.785 --> 00:07:36.310
All right, but something small.

00:07:36.354 --> 00:07:37.548
Maybe a scarf?

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:40.183
What a curious people you are.

00:07:40.225 --> 00:07:42.785
Tell me,
would it help if I said

00:07:42.827 --> 00:07:45.091
that you could have
an entire wardrobe

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.927
made from these
beautiful fabrics,

00:07:46.965 --> 00:07:49.934
and that it would give
all of us pleasure

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:51.902
to create it for you?

00:07:51.936 --> 00:07:54.404
Let's...
start with the scarf.

00:07:54.439 --> 00:07:55.963
As you like.

00:07:56.074 --> 00:07:58.838
Which cloth do you prefer, huh?

00:08:05.984 --> 00:08:08.282
That's beautiful.

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:10.514
Are you a musician?

00:08:10.555 --> 00:08:13.023
This isn't a musical instrument.

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:15.083
It's an atmospheric sensor.

00:08:15.126 --> 00:08:17.151
The frequency of the chimes

00:08:17.195 --> 00:08:20.687
indicates changes
in weather conditions.

00:08:20.732 --> 00:08:24.634
Then it must work on a principle
of non-linear resonance,

00:08:24.669 --> 00:08:27.433
adjusting to the dynamic
variables in the atmosphere.

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:29.770
That's exactly right.

00:08:29.808 --> 00:08:31.673
Are you a scientist?

00:08:31.709 --> 00:08:33.370
In a sense.

00:08:33.411 --> 00:08:35.538
Can you show me
how to operate it?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.275
I'd be happy to.

00:08:37.315 --> 00:08:41.945
First, you have to initialize
the sub-harmonic mode.

00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:46.484
Mm-hmm.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.926
Oh, I think this one.

00:08:50.962 --> 00:08:53.692
When I see you
wearing that scarf,

00:08:53.731 --> 00:08:56.598
my pleasure will be
greater than yours.

00:08:57.735 --> 00:09:00.101
Well, I should get back.

00:09:00.138 --> 00:09:01.435
But with your permission,

00:09:01.473 --> 00:09:04.806
I'd like to start
organizing teams

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:05.901
to gather plants and seeds.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.137
This is my associate,
Jaret Otel.

00:09:08.179 --> 00:09:11.637
You may contact him to make
any necessary arrangements.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:15.380
We'll be glad to assist you
in any way, Captain.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.753
I'll find my officers,
and we'll return to the ship.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.623
Tonight, we are having
a celebration here.

00:09:21.659 --> 00:09:25.117
I hope you and your officers
will be my guests.

00:09:27.098 --> 00:09:29.123
We'd be delighted.

00:09:36.474 --> 00:09:39.272
Captain's Log, Stardate 48642.5.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.938
The crew is enjoying an evening
on Sikaris.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.949
They are discovering,
to their delight, that reports

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:48.475
of this species' hospitality
have not been exaggerated.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.784
...so the whole thing exploded,

00:09:50.822 --> 00:09:54.280
and there we were,
70,000 light years from home,

00:09:54.325 --> 00:09:56.657
and no way to get back.

00:09:58.329 --> 00:10:00.229
Felt pretty lonely.

00:10:00.265 --> 00:10:02.495
That's a very noble story.

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:03.967
Noble?

00:10:04.068 --> 00:10:06.366
Mm-hmm.
Stories can be whimsical

00:10:06.404 --> 00:10:10.670
or frightening or-or melancholy
or many other things,

00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:16.010
but noble stories are the ones
that can most affect our lives.

00:10:17.515 --> 00:10:22.612
May I have your permission
to tell others this story?

00:10:22.654 --> 00:10:23.985
Sure.

00:10:24.055 --> 00:10:25.420
It's no secret.

00:10:25.456 --> 00:10:27.981
But stories are
an essential part

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:29.926
of every person's being.

00:10:29.961 --> 00:10:32.589
I would never share one
without permission.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.495
Go right ahead.

00:10:34.532 --> 00:10:36.796
I've got a few others, too.

00:10:36.834 --> 00:10:39.530
You do?

00:10:39.571 --> 00:10:41.232
Come with me.

00:10:43.707 --> 00:10:46.335
I know a private place

00:10:46.376 --> 00:10:50.210
where you can tell me
all your stories.

00:10:50.247 --> 00:10:52.215
Stand close to me.

00:10:53.884 --> 00:10:55.784
Alastria.

00:11:01.391 --> 00:11:02.756
Mm...

00:11:02.793 --> 00:11:04.420
Where are we?

00:11:04.461 --> 00:11:06.554
The woods of Alastria...

00:11:06.597 --> 00:11:08.622
my favorite place.

00:11:08.665 --> 00:11:12.157
I usually come here
when I want to spend time alone,

00:11:12.202 --> 00:11:13.430
but tonight, it...

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.303
it seemed right to bring you.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.535
Now...

00:11:18.575 --> 00:11:21.373
tell me your stories...

00:11:21.411 --> 00:11:23.003
all of them.

00:11:24.615 --> 00:11:27.743
Why is it so much warmer here?

00:11:29.219 --> 00:11:31.517
What is that?

00:11:31.555 --> 00:11:34.524
The dawn zephyr.

00:11:34.558 --> 00:11:37.220
Dawn? We just got here.

00:11:43.934 --> 00:11:46.903
That's... that is
an amazing feeling.

00:11:46.937 --> 00:11:48.802
What... what's happening?

00:11:48.839 --> 00:11:51.171
The erosene winds...

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:56.375
passion winds...

00:11:56.413 --> 00:12:00.816
come just before the dawn.

00:12:00.851 --> 00:12:03.843
The erosene creates euphoria.

00:12:07.024 --> 00:12:09.390
I'll say.

00:12:26.309 --> 00:12:28.573
Why am I seeing two suns?

00:12:28.612 --> 00:12:32.378
Because this is a binary system.

00:12:32.416 --> 00:12:35.146
But your planet
only has one sun.

00:12:35.185 --> 00:12:38.052
But Alastria has two.

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:40.522
Eudana...

00:12:40.557 --> 00:12:42.320
Hmm?

00:12:42.359 --> 00:12:43.883
Where are we?

00:12:43.927 --> 00:12:45.986
I told you...

00:12:46.029 --> 00:12:48.156
Alastria...

00:12:48.198 --> 00:12:50.826
a system far from Sikaris.

00:12:50.867 --> 00:12:52.425
How far?

00:12:52.469 --> 00:12:55.267
Do you have to ask
all these questions?

00:12:57.908 --> 00:12:59.808
Please, it's important.

00:13:00.877 --> 00:13:03.402
Alastria is about
two and a half billion times

00:13:03.447 --> 00:13:06.575
the distance
between Sikaris and its sun.

00:13:06.616 --> 00:13:09.050
That's almost...

00:13:09.086 --> 00:13:11.145
40,000 light-years.

00:13:11.188 --> 00:13:14.214
Mmm...

00:13:14.257 --> 00:13:15.451
Now...

00:13:17.594 --> 00:13:19.585
...feel the breeze.

00:13:22.933 --> 00:13:25.265
Um, we have to go back.

00:13:25.302 --> 00:13:27.361
It's still night on Sikaris.

00:13:27.404 --> 00:13:29.133
We have plenty of time.

00:13:31.174 --> 00:13:33.142
No. Um...

00:13:33.176 --> 00:13:35.201
we're going back...

00:13:35.245 --> 00:13:38.305
and I need you
to tell me everything you know

00:13:38.348 --> 00:13:40.908
about that platform
that got us here.

00:13:40.951 --> 00:13:46.856
And tomorrow night, you must
let me take you to the theater.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.118
Oh, my.

00:13:48.158 --> 00:13:50.217
I have lost all track of time.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.488
My crew has gone.

00:13:51.528 --> 00:13:53.189
I'm the last one here.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:57.860
I hope that's because
you are enjoying yourself.

00:13:57.901 --> 00:13:59.232
I am.

00:14:03.306 --> 00:14:04.705
Captain!

00:14:04.741 --> 00:14:06.436
Excuse me for interrupting,

00:14:06.476 --> 00:14:08.341
but I've just found out
about something incredible.

00:14:08.378 --> 00:14:09.345
Calm down, Ensign.

00:14:09.379 --> 00:14:10.641
What is it?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.114
That platform...

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:14.947
it's a transportation device.

00:14:14.985 --> 00:14:16.782
Extremely sophisticated.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.947
It operates on the principle
of folding space.

00:14:19.022 --> 00:14:22.651
That's something
that's been theorized,

00:14:22.692 --> 00:14:26.321
but no one's ever been able
to develop the technology.

00:14:26.363 --> 00:14:28.160
Well, these people have.

00:14:28.198 --> 00:14:31.634
I've just been
to Alastria and back.

00:14:31.668 --> 00:14:35.104
Alastria is 40,000
light years away.

00:14:36.139 --> 00:14:38.801
We call it a spatial trajector.

00:14:38.842 --> 00:14:40.309
We're able to travel

00:14:40.343 --> 00:14:41.970
to all the planets
in this Quadrant.

00:14:42.078 --> 00:14:44.171
How far can it take you?

00:14:44.214 --> 00:14:46.978
Alastria is at the outermost
limits of its range.

00:14:47.017 --> 00:14:48.177
Apparently, it's

00:14:48.218 --> 00:14:50.686
never been used to move anything
as large as Voyager,

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.087
but as I understand
the principle of space folding,

00:14:54.124 --> 00:14:56.718
the size of the object
isn't relevant.

00:14:57.761 --> 00:14:59.592
What do you think?

00:14:59.629 --> 00:15:02.894
Would it be possible
to modify your technology

00:15:02.933 --> 00:15:05.493
so we could use it?

00:15:05.535 --> 00:15:07.264
I tried to tell him.

00:15:07.304 --> 00:15:09.067
What is it?

00:15:09.105 --> 00:15:11.039
We cannot share our technology.

00:15:11.074 --> 00:15:12.541
Once it's out of our control,

00:15:12.576 --> 00:15:15.841
it might fall into the hands
of those who would abuse it,

00:15:15.879 --> 00:15:19.371
and our Canon of Laws
strictly forbids that.

00:15:19.416 --> 00:15:21.043
But we wouldn't abuse it.

00:15:21.084 --> 00:15:24.815
Don't you see
what it would mean to us?

00:15:24.855 --> 00:15:27.619
Please, don't make it
more difficult for me.

00:15:27.657 --> 00:15:29.625
I don't enjoy denying you this,

00:15:29.659 --> 00:15:32.059
but our Canon of Laws
has determined

00:15:32.095 --> 00:15:33.858
our entire system of values.

00:15:33.897 --> 00:15:36.263
To break one of its precepts

00:15:36.299 --> 00:15:39.496
would undermine
everything we believe in.

00:15:39.536 --> 00:15:44.269
I'm sorry, but there can be
no exceptions to the law.

00:15:59.789 --> 00:16:02.815
I can't believe
they're not going to help us.

00:16:02.859 --> 00:16:04.588
Some kind of hospitality.

00:16:04.628 --> 00:16:05.788
40,000 light years.

00:16:05.829 --> 00:16:08.127
Even if that's
as far as we could go,

00:16:08.164 --> 00:16:11.258
it would still knock
about four decades off our trip.

00:16:11.301 --> 00:16:12.563
And the possibility exists

00:16:12.602 --> 00:16:14.502
that we could reconfigure
the matrix at that point,

00:16:14.537 --> 00:16:16.437
to take us another
30,000 light-years,

00:16:16.473 --> 00:16:18.805
right into Federation space.

00:16:18.842 --> 00:16:20.366
Since they've already said no,

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.275
this kind of thinking
is only going

00:16:22.312 --> 00:16:23.939
to make you feel worse.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:27.746
It's the first time
we've been on the other side

00:16:27.784 --> 00:16:29.308
of the fence.

00:16:29.352 --> 00:16:30.683
What fence?

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.484
The one that's made
of binding principles.

00:16:33.523 --> 00:16:35.514
We have our own set of rules

00:16:35.558 --> 00:16:38.618
which includes
the Prime Directive.

00:16:38.662 --> 00:16:40.630
How many times
have we been in the position

00:16:40.664 --> 00:16:43.633
of refusing to interfere
when some kind of disaster

00:16:43.667 --> 00:16:45.828
threatened an alien culture?

00:16:45.869 --> 00:16:48.133
It's all very well
to say we do it

00:16:48.171 --> 00:16:50.731
on the basis
of an enlightened principle,

00:16:50.774 --> 00:16:53.242
but how does that feel
to the aliens?

00:16:55.512 --> 00:16:57.309
I'm sure many of them think

00:16:57.347 --> 00:16:59.815
the Prime Directive
is a lousy idea.

00:16:59.849 --> 00:17:01.146
Even we think so sometimes.

00:17:01.184 --> 00:17:03.243
I know of many times
when Starfleet personnel

00:17:03.286 --> 00:17:06.119
have decided on strong
ethical grounds to ignore it.

00:17:06.156 --> 00:17:07.453
Still, there's a reason

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.754
why it's Starfleet's
General Order #1.

00:17:09.793 --> 00:17:11.590
On the whole, it does
a lot more good than harm.

00:17:11.628 --> 00:17:13.061
Captain, it occurs to me

00:17:13.096 --> 00:17:15.087
that we know little
about the Sikarians.

00:17:15.131 --> 00:17:16.257
We cannot assume

00:17:16.299 --> 00:17:18.597
that their first refusal
is unalterable.

00:17:18.635 --> 00:17:21.604
It may be that "no" is simply
a prelude to negotiation.

00:17:21.638 --> 00:17:23.936
He's right.
Maybe they can be reasoned with.

00:17:23.974 --> 00:17:24.941
Maybe they want something.

00:17:24.975 --> 00:17:26.272
Maybe they'll bargain.

00:17:26.309 --> 00:17:27.936
But what do we have to offer?

00:17:27.978 --> 00:17:30.310
They seem to have
everything they need.

00:17:33.149 --> 00:17:34.514
Stories.

00:17:34.551 --> 00:17:37.952
Stories are an important part
of their culture.

00:17:37.988 --> 00:17:40.354
They seem to provide
more than entertainment.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:43.553
They're kind of a measuring rod
of values and beliefs.

00:17:43.593 --> 00:17:46.161
We have a huge library
in our data banks.

00:17:46.294 --> 00:17:47.886
We could offer them
the whole thing.

00:17:47.929 --> 00:17:50.227
All the great literature
of dozens of cultures.

00:17:50.265 --> 00:17:51.596
What do you think, Captain?

00:17:51.633 --> 00:17:52.895
Would they be interested?

00:17:52.934 --> 00:17:55.368
They just might be.

00:17:57.138 --> 00:17:59.106
From what we've seen of them,

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.439
they're a remarkably
pleasure-oriented people.

00:18:02.477 --> 00:18:06.413
They might appreciate
a gift of literature.

00:18:06.447 --> 00:18:07.812
I'll arrange to meet with Gath.

00:18:07.849 --> 00:18:10.579
As magistrate, he has the
authority to make this decision.

00:18:10.618 --> 00:18:11.915
In the meantime,

00:18:11.953 --> 00:18:14.319
I'm going to take a look
at that trajector platform.

00:18:14.355 --> 00:18:15.913
Maybe I can figure out
how it works.

00:18:16.024 --> 00:18:17.958
You'll do nothing of the sort,
Lieutenant.

00:18:20.962 --> 00:18:22.429
If I find
this law is negotiable,

00:18:22.463 --> 00:18:25.432
I'll make every attempt
to get the technology,

00:18:25.466 --> 00:18:28.333
but until then, we won't do
anything that might violate

00:18:28.369 --> 00:18:31.497
their Canon of Laws
as we understand it.

00:18:31.539 --> 00:18:33.336
That's all.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:44.142
What's wrong?

00:18:46.921 --> 00:18:49.583
I just hope she gets it.

00:18:51.359 --> 00:18:53.452
She will.

00:19:03.438 --> 00:19:05.429
Mmm. Exquisite.

00:19:05.473 --> 00:19:08.135
And what did you say
you call it?

00:19:08.176 --> 00:19:10.167
Pecan pie.

00:19:10.211 --> 00:19:11.701
I must have the recipe.

00:19:11.746 --> 00:19:14.010
I'd be happy
to share it with you.

00:19:18.052 --> 00:19:21.317
Gath... I want you to know
I understand your reluctance

00:19:21.356 --> 00:19:23.381
to share your technology
with us.

00:19:23.424 --> 00:19:24.914
We have similar restrictions.

00:19:25.026 --> 00:19:27.517
But I wondered,

00:19:27.562 --> 00:19:29.792
would it make any difference
if I gave you my word

00:19:29.831 --> 00:19:31.696
that we would destroy
the trajector matrix

00:19:31.733 --> 00:19:33.894
as soon as we'd used it?

00:19:33.935 --> 00:19:37.803
I know this will upset you,
but I can't.

00:19:37.839 --> 00:19:42.208
I understand, and frankly,
I suspected as much,

00:19:42.243 --> 00:19:46.441
but I have a proposal
which might allow you

00:19:46.481 --> 00:19:48.176
to obey your laws

00:19:48.216 --> 00:19:51.014
and still give us what we want.

00:19:54.289 --> 00:19:57.315
Surely you could use
the trajector to send us.

00:19:57.358 --> 00:20:01.590
40,000 light-years
would mean a great deal to us,

00:20:01.629 --> 00:20:05.759
and in return, we're prepared
to offer you something

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.062
you might enjoy.

00:20:07.101 --> 00:20:08.466
Oh!

00:20:08.503 --> 00:20:09.970
A full library

00:20:10.004 --> 00:20:14.270
of the Federation's
finest literature.

00:20:14.309 --> 00:20:16.174
Literature?

00:20:18.579 --> 00:20:20.672
Centuries of stories.

00:20:20.715 --> 00:20:23.878
New stories
from diverse cultures.

00:20:23.918 --> 00:20:26.443
Stories that fire
the imagination.

00:20:28.256 --> 00:20:32.989
You certainly know
how to tempt me, Captain.

00:20:33.061 --> 00:20:35.529
It's certainly possible.

00:20:35.563 --> 00:20:38.225
I'll have to meet with the other
magistrates to discuss it.

00:20:38.266 --> 00:20:40.996
No one has ever made
a request like that.

00:20:41.069 --> 00:20:45.836
In the meantime, I'd like to
enjoy every bite of, uh, this...

00:20:45.873 --> 00:20:47.602
how did you call it?

00:20:47.642 --> 00:20:49.234
Pecan pie.

00:20:59.053 --> 00:21:00.987
I finished the maintenance check

00:21:01.022 --> 00:21:03.115
on the shock attenuation
cylinders.

00:21:03.157 --> 00:21:05.284
They'll have to be replaced
in another 2,000 hours,

00:21:05.326 --> 00:21:07.988
but we'll face that problem
when we come to it.

00:21:09.831 --> 00:21:11.298
Seska.

00:21:11.332 --> 00:21:13.960
Sorry. I wasn't concentrating.

00:21:14.001 --> 00:21:16.629
What did you say?

00:21:16.671 --> 00:21:19.606
You looked a million
light-years away.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:20.766
No.

00:21:20.808 --> 00:21:23.971
Only about 70,000.

00:21:24.078 --> 00:21:28.742
My brother's birthday
is in four days.

00:21:28.783 --> 00:21:32.310
Last year, I promised
I'd meet him on Nivoch

00:21:32.353 --> 00:21:34.583
to celebrate with him.

00:21:34.622 --> 00:21:37.022
He'll think I broke my promise.

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:41.228
That I'm dead.

00:21:50.505 --> 00:21:51.494
What are you doing?

00:21:51.539 --> 00:21:52.597
I've been thinking.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:55.473
The folding of space
should leave a subspace residue.

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:56.602
If we can detect one,

00:21:56.644 --> 00:21:58.544
we might be a step closer
to knowing

00:21:58.579 --> 00:21:59.910
how the trajector works.

00:21:59.947 --> 00:22:02.142
Look at that
neutrino dispersion pattern.

00:22:02.183 --> 00:22:05.209
Could that be the result
of space folding?

00:22:05.253 --> 00:22:08.347
Maybe. If the device
creates a neutrino bubble

00:22:08.389 --> 00:22:10.721
around whatever's
being trajected.

00:22:10.758 --> 00:22:12.225
If that's the case,

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:15.229
we'd need a bubble
big enough for the ship.

00:22:15.263 --> 00:22:18.061
Don't worry, Lieutenant.

00:22:18.099 --> 00:22:20.567
I'm with you on this one.

00:22:20.601 --> 00:22:24.537
After all,
it doesn't hurt to theorize.

00:22:24.572 --> 00:22:29.475
Right, and hypothetically,

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:31.944
if we could modify
the deflector array

00:22:31.979 --> 00:22:33.640
to emit phased neutrinos,

00:22:33.681 --> 00:22:36.479
we could create
a big enough bubble.

00:22:36.517 --> 00:22:37.848
Let's give it a try.

00:22:37.885 --> 00:22:39.944
In theory, of course.

00:22:49.363 --> 00:22:50.660
I don't understand.

00:22:50.698 --> 00:22:52.495
Why is it so important
I come here now?

00:22:52.533 --> 00:22:54.524
You'll see in a minute.

00:22:59.407 --> 00:23:00.772
We're here.

00:23:00.808 --> 00:23:01.934
Good evening, Ensign.

00:23:01.976 --> 00:23:03.944
Thank you for coming.

00:23:03.978 --> 00:23:05.275
What's this about?

00:23:05.313 --> 00:23:06.610
I asked Eudana
to invite you here

00:23:06.647 --> 00:23:09.241
because I was sure
you would respond to her

00:23:09.283 --> 00:23:11.945
and because it would
look perfectly natural.

00:23:12.019 --> 00:23:14.886
I am prepared to accept
your collection of literature

00:23:14.922 --> 00:23:17.117
in exchange
for our trajector technology.

00:23:17.158 --> 00:23:20.252
Is that something
you're authorized to do?

00:23:20.294 --> 00:23:23.457
Officially, no,
but many people believe

00:23:23.498 --> 00:23:25.557
that rules
should be flexible enough

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:28.398
to meet the needs of the moment.

00:23:28.436 --> 00:23:31.098
There is a great desire here
for new stories,

00:23:31.138 --> 00:23:33.663
and I want to be the one
to supply them.

00:23:33.708 --> 00:23:37.474
So you'd stand to benefit
from this arrangement, right?

00:23:37.512 --> 00:23:39.241
We would both benefit.

00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:40.941
I would gain prestige,

00:23:40.982 --> 00:23:43.917
and you would gain
40,000 light-years

00:23:43.951 --> 00:23:48.149
in your journey home,
possibly more.

00:23:48.189 --> 00:23:49.315
This is it, Ensign...

00:23:49.357 --> 00:23:50.688
the matrix of the trajector.

00:23:54.428 --> 00:23:56.760
Captain Janeway
has asked the magistrate

00:23:56.797 --> 00:23:58.321
to send us 40,000 light-years.

00:23:58.366 --> 00:23:59.765
He won't.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:02.360
He never had any intention
of helping you leave here.

00:24:02.403 --> 00:24:04.268
Jaret is right.

00:24:04.305 --> 00:24:08.366
I know how much
it means to you to get home.

00:24:08.409 --> 00:24:10.536
Please, listen to him.

00:24:10.578 --> 00:24:12.637
You must believe me
when I tell you

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:15.547
this is the only way
you will make that journey.

00:24:17.418 --> 00:24:19.909
Consider my offer.

00:24:19.954 --> 00:24:22.718
I'm sure you will decide
it is a fair one.

00:24:22.757 --> 00:24:25.954
I don't know what to do.

00:24:25.993 --> 00:24:29.292
I know we'd all like to get
that much closer to home,

00:24:29.330 --> 00:24:30.627
but I don't think
Captain Janeway

00:24:30.665 --> 00:24:32.792
is going to go for getting
the technology like that.

00:24:32.833 --> 00:24:34.460
Maybe she will.

00:24:34.502 --> 00:24:37.562
After all, it's a Sikarian
who's making the offer.

00:24:37.605 --> 00:24:39.163
But it's not aboveboard.

00:24:39.206 --> 00:24:41.401
The Captain
is only going to deal

00:24:41.442 --> 00:24:43.740
with an official representative.

00:24:43.778 --> 00:24:44.767
Bridge to Ensign Kim.

00:24:44.812 --> 00:24:46.246
The Captain can see you now.

00:24:46.379 --> 00:24:47.607
Just tell her
everything you know.

00:24:47.647 --> 00:24:48.807
Let her take it from there.

00:24:48.848 --> 00:24:50.713
Right.

00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:52.377
I'll walk you partway.

00:24:52.418 --> 00:24:54.318
I'm headed for bed.

00:24:55.688 --> 00:25:00.489
Somehow... I have
a bad feeling about this.

00:25:00.526 --> 00:25:01.925
It's just not going to work out.

00:25:01.961 --> 00:25:05.260
Don't you think that's up to us?

00:25:05.298 --> 00:25:06.925
What does that mean?

00:25:06.966 --> 00:25:08.661
It means that we can sit here

00:25:08.701 --> 00:25:10.328
and let someone make
the decision for us,

00:25:10.370 --> 00:25:11.928
or we can take matters
into our own hands.

00:25:12.038 --> 00:25:14.905
We've been offered
the grand prize.

00:25:14.941 --> 00:25:17.273
All we have to do is
step up and claim it.

00:25:17.310 --> 00:25:19.710
Take the technology?

00:25:19.746 --> 00:25:21.338
Without permission?

00:25:21.381 --> 00:25:23.645
Since when
do you talk like that?

00:25:23.683 --> 00:25:25.617
Do you think permission
is more important

00:25:25.652 --> 00:25:28.450
than getting us halfway home?

00:25:28.488 --> 00:25:32.083
The Captain is so infatuated
with the Sikarian magistrate,

00:25:32.125 --> 00:25:33.558
she can't think straight.

00:25:33.593 --> 00:25:35.117
We can't trust
that she's going to make

00:25:35.161 --> 00:25:38.619
the best decision for all of us.

00:25:38.665 --> 00:25:41.133
If we do this,
we'll need to use Engineering

00:25:41.167 --> 00:25:43.533
to configure the matrix.

00:25:43.569 --> 00:25:46.538
It will be a lot easier if we
knew we could count on you.

00:25:46.572 --> 00:25:49.473
Seska, I am
a senior officer now.

00:25:49.509 --> 00:25:51.409
I have responsibilities.

00:25:51.444 --> 00:25:53.378
And the main responsibility
for everyone on this ship

00:25:53.413 --> 00:25:54.471
is to try to find a way home.

00:25:54.514 --> 00:25:57.574
Captain Janeway made that clear
from the beginning.

00:25:57.617 --> 00:26:00.745
That's our primary mission.

00:26:00.787 --> 00:26:03.119
Just think about it.

00:26:03.156 --> 00:26:05.454
That's all.

00:26:18.871 --> 00:26:20.839
Did Jaret explain what he meant
when he said

00:26:20.873 --> 00:26:22.773
Gath had no intention
of helping us leave?

00:26:22.809 --> 00:26:23.935
No.

00:26:24.010 --> 00:26:26.274
He just made it clear
that our only choice

00:26:26.312 --> 00:26:28.280
was to get the trajector
technology from him.

00:26:28.314 --> 00:26:31.613
He may simply want us to believe
that so we would deal with him.

00:26:32.652 --> 00:26:34.950
Possibly...

00:26:34.987 --> 00:26:38.946
but somehow,
I suspect he's right.

00:26:38.991 --> 00:26:40.788
Thank you for coming to me
with this, Ensign.

00:26:40.827 --> 00:26:42.954
It may muddy
the situation somewhat,

00:26:42.995 --> 00:26:44.826
but it helps me force the issue.

00:26:44.864 --> 00:26:46.092
Dismissed.

00:26:46.132 --> 00:26:47.724
Good night, Captain.

00:26:47.767 --> 00:26:49.098
Lieutenant.

00:26:55.108 --> 00:26:58.134
Oh, Tuvok, what do I do now?

00:26:58.177 --> 00:27:00.805
You would seem
to have two options...

00:27:00.847 --> 00:27:04.908
continue to negotiate with a man
who may have a hidden agenda,

00:27:04.984 --> 00:27:09.250
or deal with a man who is
willing to defy his own laws.

00:27:09.288 --> 00:27:11.256
Not very pretty choices.

00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:13.656
At least if you deal with Jaret,

00:27:13.693 --> 00:27:15.593
it is his law
that is being compromised,

00:27:15.628 --> 00:27:19.086
not ours.

00:27:19.132 --> 00:27:21.600
But does that matter?

00:27:21.634 --> 00:27:23.932
I told the crew
when we started this journey

00:27:23.970 --> 00:27:26.097
that we'd be a Starfleet crew,

00:27:26.139 --> 00:27:28.801
behaving as Starfleet
would expect us to.

00:27:28.841 --> 00:27:32.538
That means there's a certain
standard I have to uphold.

00:27:33.946 --> 00:27:36.608
Principles, principles.

00:27:36.649 --> 00:27:39.618
That's what it comes down to.

00:27:39.652 --> 00:27:43.713
Do I compromise
my almighty principles?

00:27:43.756 --> 00:27:46.316
But how do I not compromise them

00:27:46.359 --> 00:27:48.759
if it involves a chance
to get the crew

00:27:48.795 --> 00:27:51.559
more than halfway home?

00:27:51.597 --> 00:27:53.895
How do I tell them...

00:27:53.933 --> 00:27:56.868
my principles are so important

00:27:56.903 --> 00:27:59.497
I would deny them
that opportunity?

00:28:01.674 --> 00:28:03.767
I believe
the first thing you must do

00:28:03.810 --> 00:28:05.107
is determine whether or not

00:28:05.144 --> 00:28:08.238
Gath is willing to use
the trajector to help us.

00:28:08.281 --> 00:28:10.249
If that possibility
exists at all,

00:28:10.283 --> 00:28:11.910
you must explore it.

00:28:11.951 --> 00:28:13.612
You're right.

00:28:17.623 --> 00:28:19.818
Thank you, Tuvok.

00:28:23.896 --> 00:28:26.592
Have you spoken
with the other magistrates

00:28:26.632 --> 00:28:28.930
about using the trajector?

00:28:28.968 --> 00:28:30.595
Actually, I haven't.

00:28:30.636 --> 00:28:31.466
Some of them are traveling now,

00:28:31.504 --> 00:28:34.769
but I assure you I will do it.

00:28:34.807 --> 00:28:38.265
Oh, I've already seen all those.

00:28:38.311 --> 00:28:40.939
It's becoming a matter
of some urgency.

00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:42.277
Oh. Why?

00:28:42.315 --> 00:28:44.613
We've imposed on you
for long enough.

00:28:44.650 --> 00:28:46.208
Not true.

00:28:46.252 --> 00:28:49.312
We welcome you
for as long as you can stay,

00:28:49.355 --> 00:28:52.483
and I hope that's
a very long time indeed.

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:57.787
My crew is eager
to continue our journey.

00:28:57.830 --> 00:28:59.388
Once they realized

00:28:59.432 --> 00:29:01.627
the trajector might bring
us 40,000 light-years

00:29:01.667 --> 00:29:03.134
closer to home...

00:29:03.169 --> 00:29:06.605
Why are you so consumed
with this desire to get home?

00:29:06.639 --> 00:29:09.107
I find it difficult
to understand.

00:29:09.141 --> 00:29:12.076
Home... is home.

00:29:12.111 --> 00:29:14.272
It's where we belong.

00:29:14.313 --> 00:29:17.510
Couldn't you create
a new home here with us?

00:29:17.550 --> 00:29:20.041
Can you imagine
a more delightful place to live

00:29:20.086 --> 00:29:22.748
where you could pass your time
extracting pleasure

00:29:22.788 --> 00:29:24.346
from every moment?

00:29:24.390 --> 00:29:25.914
I promise you,

00:29:25.958 --> 00:29:30.588
you and I have many
such moments to explore.

00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:35.431
Yes, but for how long?

00:29:35.468 --> 00:29:38.596
I've seen how quickly
you get tired of your pleasures.

00:29:38.638 --> 00:29:42.938
All that interests you
is what's new and unexplored.

00:29:43.009 --> 00:29:46.103
After a day or two,
it becomes commonplace.

00:29:46.145 --> 00:29:47.772
Yes...

00:29:47.813 --> 00:29:50.145
We prefer permanence...

00:29:50.182 --> 00:29:53.117
the reward
of relationships that endure

00:29:53.152 --> 00:29:55.950
and grow deeper
with the passing of time.

00:29:55.988 --> 00:29:59.754
You would lose those notions
if you stayed with us.

00:29:59.792 --> 00:30:04.422
You may be right,
and that's why we have to leave.

00:30:06.499 --> 00:30:09.127
We have offered you
nothing but hospitality.

00:30:09.168 --> 00:30:14.333
Is this how you repay us,
with an attack on our beliefs?

00:30:14.373 --> 00:30:16.933
I'm sorry.

00:30:16.976 --> 00:30:20.639
I was just trying to illustrate
the differences between us.

00:30:20.680 --> 00:30:22.807
I don't enjoy
being judged like this.

00:30:22.848 --> 00:30:25.442
It's very upsetting,
not at all pleasurable.

00:30:26.485 --> 00:30:30.319
That's all you really
care about, isn't it?

00:30:30.356 --> 00:30:32.153
Your pleasure.

00:30:32.191 --> 00:30:36.287
All your hospitality,
your graciousness...

00:30:36.329 --> 00:30:39.492
it was never
about giving us pleasure.

00:30:39.532 --> 00:30:42.990
It's all been
to gratify yourselves.

00:30:43.069 --> 00:30:45.867
We're nothing more
than the latest novelty.

00:30:45.905 --> 00:30:49.170
You're hostile and vicious.

00:30:49.208 --> 00:30:51.676
You would infect
the joyousness of our lives.

00:30:51.711 --> 00:30:53.702
You must leave immediately.

00:30:55.381 --> 00:30:58.214
You never had any intention
of helping us, did you?

00:30:58.250 --> 00:30:59.547
Of course I did.

00:30:59.585 --> 00:31:02.281
I did everything in my power
to persuade you to stay here.

00:31:03.990 --> 00:31:05.617
Janeway to Voyager.

00:31:05.658 --> 00:31:07.489
One to beam up.

00:31:18.337 --> 00:31:21.204
Cancel all shore leave
and recall the away teams.

00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:23.140
We've been asked to leave.

00:31:23.175 --> 00:31:24.665
Aye, Captain.

00:31:26.345 --> 00:31:29.644
I assume that means
Gath will not be assisting us.

00:31:29.682 --> 00:31:32.480
I don't think he ever had
any intention of helping us.

00:31:32.518 --> 00:31:35.646
He just... strung us along.

00:31:35.688 --> 00:31:38.156
Are you considering
Jaret's offer?

00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:40.658
Oh, I wish I could...

00:31:40.693 --> 00:31:42.661
but I can't.

00:31:42.695 --> 00:31:45.129
Captain, it'll take hours
to get everyone up.

00:31:45.164 --> 00:31:46.290
We've got crew members

00:31:46.332 --> 00:31:48.000
scattered throughout
both hemispheres.

00:31:48.133 --> 00:31:50.328
Get them back as quickly
as you can, Commander.

00:31:50.369 --> 00:31:52.496
I think we've overextended
our stay here.

00:31:52.537 --> 00:31:55.472
I'll be in my ready room.

00:32:01.146 --> 00:32:03.273
I've downloaded
the Federation library.

00:32:03.315 --> 00:32:05.283
It all on these chips.

00:32:05.317 --> 00:32:06.614
We know the man to contact.

00:32:06.651 --> 00:32:07.948
He wants the library,

00:32:07.986 --> 00:32:09.954
and he doesn't care
who gives it to him.

00:32:09.988 --> 00:32:10.955
We're under orders...

00:32:10.989 --> 00:32:12.786
B'Elanna, right now,

00:32:12.824 --> 00:32:14.951
our people are still
fighting Cardassians,

00:32:14.993 --> 00:32:16.961
dying for our cause.

00:32:16.995 --> 00:32:19.190
Settlers
in the Demilitarized Zone

00:32:19.231 --> 00:32:20.926
are still under attack.

00:32:20.966 --> 00:32:22.934
We made a promise, B'Elanna,

00:32:22.968 --> 00:32:26.199
that we'd all stick together
until the Zone was safe,

00:32:26.238 --> 00:32:29.207
and I intend
to keep that promise.

00:32:29.241 --> 00:32:32.472
I have a wife
and two little boys.

00:32:32.511 --> 00:32:34.638
I don't want them to grow up
without a father.

00:32:34.679 --> 00:32:36.977
I'd do anything to prevent that.

00:32:37.082 --> 00:32:39.073
We're not the only ones.

00:32:39.117 --> 00:32:41.449
Everyone wants to get back.

00:32:41.486 --> 00:32:44.182
They're just waiting
for someone to act.

00:32:44.222 --> 00:32:46.782
I've been working on the theory
that the trajector

00:32:46.825 --> 00:32:48.986
operates
within a neutrino envelope.

00:32:49.094 --> 00:32:49.992
If that's true,

00:32:50.095 --> 00:32:53.622
I think we can use it
as many times as we need

00:32:53.665 --> 00:32:56.259
until we're all the way home.

00:32:56.301 --> 00:33:00.567
Just think... by tomorrow,
we could be there.

00:33:05.644 --> 00:33:08.943
All right.

00:33:08.980 --> 00:33:10.607
Let's do it.

00:33:16.988 --> 00:33:18.717
With shore leave canceled,

00:33:18.757 --> 00:33:20.952
are we able to get
to the surface undetected?

00:33:20.992 --> 00:33:23.119
We'll have to override
the security lockout,

00:33:23.161 --> 00:33:24.287
but that shouldn't
be a problem.

00:33:24.329 --> 00:33:26.456
It's not accepting
my security code.

00:33:26.498 --> 00:33:28.125
Reinitialize
the lockout buffers.

00:33:28.166 --> 00:33:29.064
I did.
It's not working.

00:33:29.101 --> 00:33:30.796
Someone's altered
the security subroutine.

00:33:30.836 --> 00:33:31.962
Why would anyone do that?

00:33:32.003 --> 00:33:33.800
Never mind.
Beam me down.

00:33:33.839 --> 00:33:35.306
Are you crazy?!

00:33:35.340 --> 00:33:38.173
Security will find you out
before you get there.

00:33:46.451 --> 00:33:49.477
I altered
the security subroutines.

00:33:49.521 --> 00:33:51.989
Any attempt to override
the lockout

00:33:52.023 --> 00:33:54.150
would have alerted me
to your presence here.

00:34:00.332 --> 00:34:02.630
Is this Voyager's library

00:34:02.667 --> 00:34:05.898
which you intended to trade
for the trajector technology?

00:34:07.139 --> 00:34:08.731
Yes.

00:34:11.309 --> 00:34:13.277
When I attempted to download it,

00:34:13.311 --> 00:34:15.211
I noticed it had
already been accessed.

00:34:15.247 --> 00:34:17.647
You were going to download it?

00:34:17.682 --> 00:34:20.310
I will make the exchange
with Jaret Otel.

00:34:25.323 --> 00:34:26.950
Return to your stations.

00:34:26.992 --> 00:34:28.152
Do what you can

00:34:28.193 --> 00:34:30.184
to prepare the ship
for the matrix.

00:34:30.228 --> 00:34:32.287
Energize.

00:34:46.845 --> 00:34:48.972
Mr. Tuvok is
on the surface now, Captain.

00:34:49.014 --> 00:34:50.481
He says the remaining away teams

00:34:50.515 --> 00:34:51.948
should be on board
within 15 minutes.

00:34:51.983 --> 00:34:53.883
Are all the food supplies
secured?

00:34:53.919 --> 00:34:55.147
Aye, Captain.

00:34:55.187 --> 00:34:56.654
As soon as the last
of the crew gets back,

00:34:56.688 --> 00:34:58.155
we'll be ready to leave.

00:34:58.190 --> 00:34:59.316
Bridge to Engineering.

00:34:59.357 --> 00:35:00.551
Torres here.

00:35:00.592 --> 00:35:02.423
We'll be leaving orbit
within minutes.

00:35:02.460 --> 00:35:04.325
Ready all propulsion systems.

00:35:04.362 --> 00:35:05.989
We're ready now, Captain.

00:35:07.699 --> 00:35:08.927
Where's Tuvok?

00:35:09.034 --> 00:35:10.092
He'll be here.

00:35:10.135 --> 00:35:11.568
We certainly won't leave
without him.

00:35:11.603 --> 00:35:11.932
Well, what's keeping him?

00:35:12.037 --> 00:35:13.937
Calm down.

00:35:13.972 --> 00:35:17.135
You're going to draw
attention to yourself.

00:35:22.347 --> 00:35:24.577
Do not attempt
to activate the device

00:35:24.616 --> 00:35:26.481
until I've spoken
to Captain Janeway.

00:35:32.023 --> 00:35:33.490
What are you doing?

00:35:33.525 --> 00:35:35.550
He said not to activate it.

00:35:35.594 --> 00:35:36.822
I'm not.

00:35:36.861 --> 00:35:39.921
I'm just going to try
the interface simulation.

00:35:39.965 --> 00:35:42.456
We don't even know
if it will interface.

00:35:42.500 --> 00:35:45.958
We can give ourselves
a head start by testing it now.

00:35:46.037 --> 00:35:48.130
All right.

00:35:48.173 --> 00:35:50.835
But just a simulation.

00:35:58.350 --> 00:36:00.477
It's working.

00:36:00.518 --> 00:36:02.076
I was right.

00:36:02.120 --> 00:36:04.281
It operates
within a neutrino envelope.

00:36:04.322 --> 00:36:05.914
The trajector field
is bigger than anything

00:36:06.024 --> 00:36:08.185
we've created
by ten orders of magnitude.

00:36:08.226 --> 00:36:10.091
To get a field that size,

00:36:10.128 --> 00:36:12.619
you'd need an amplifier
as big as a planet.

00:36:12.664 --> 00:36:13.926
I don't understand.

00:36:13.999 --> 00:36:16.365
How do they get
that kind of amplification?

00:36:16.401 --> 00:36:19.063
I'll show you.

00:36:19.104 --> 00:36:20.571
Sikaris has a mantle

00:36:20.605 --> 00:36:23.938
of tetrahedral quartz
20 kilometers thick.

00:36:23.975 --> 00:36:25.806
The crystalline structure
of the mantle serves

00:36:25.844 --> 00:36:28.312
to focus and amplify
the trajector field.

00:36:28.346 --> 00:36:30.644
If that's
how the power transfer occurs,

00:36:30.682 --> 00:36:34.118
then once we leave orbit,
we lose the ability to traject.

00:36:34.152 --> 00:36:36.746
We don't have time to test it.

00:36:36.788 --> 00:36:40.280
We'll have to try it now
or forget it.

00:36:40.325 --> 00:36:41.622
- Do it.
- Lf there are

00:36:41.660 --> 00:36:43.685
- any compatibility problems...
- Then we can abort.

00:36:43.728 --> 00:36:45.628
This is our only chance.

00:36:45.664 --> 00:36:48.963
Bridge to Engineering.

00:36:49.034 --> 00:36:50.228
Torres here.

00:36:50.268 --> 00:36:51.292
We're ready to leave orbit.

00:36:51.336 --> 00:36:52.826
Thrusters on line.

00:36:52.871 --> 00:36:53.963
Aye, Captain.

00:36:54.072 --> 00:36:56.233
We have to do something.

00:36:57.809 --> 00:37:00.107
Mr. Paris, take us out of orbit.

00:37:00.145 --> 00:37:01.442
4,000 kph.

00:37:01.479 --> 00:37:03.071
Aye, Captain.

00:37:05.083 --> 00:37:06.414
There's no response.

00:37:06.451 --> 00:37:08.009
Thrusters are off line.

00:37:08.053 --> 00:37:09.611
Janeway to Engineering.

00:37:09.654 --> 00:37:11.246
What's going on, Lieutenant?

00:37:11.289 --> 00:37:14.258
We've got a phase variance
in plasma conduit 3.

00:37:14.292 --> 00:37:17.659
I'll have to check it out
before we can engage thrusters.

00:37:17.696 --> 00:37:19.459
When did this problem show up?

00:37:19.497 --> 00:37:20.930
Just now, Captain.

00:37:20.999 --> 00:37:23.832
It's only a slight variance.
I'll have it fixed in a minute.

00:37:23.868 --> 00:37:25.529
Keep me advised.

00:37:27.539 --> 00:37:29.131
All right.

00:37:29.174 --> 00:37:31.665
The matrix is activating.

00:37:31.710 --> 00:37:33.837
The trajector field is forming.

00:37:33.878 --> 00:37:35.505
And it's amplifying.

00:37:35.547 --> 00:37:37.845
Look how fast it's expanding.

00:37:37.882 --> 00:37:39.406
That's the effect
of the quartz mantle.

00:37:39.451 --> 00:37:41.351
We're nearly
at full field strength.

00:37:41.386 --> 00:37:42.353
This is going to work.

00:37:44.222 --> 00:37:45.746
What is it?

00:37:47.492 --> 00:37:49.860
The plasma manifold
is becoming unstable.

00:37:49.993 --> 00:37:51.722
I can compensate for that.

00:37:51.761 --> 00:37:53.888
The manifold is being bombarded

00:37:53.930 --> 00:37:56.296
by anti-neutrinos
from the trajector field.

00:37:56.333 --> 00:37:57.800
Anti-neutrinos?

00:37:57.834 --> 00:38:00.598
The must be the catalyst
for the space folding process.

00:38:00.637 --> 00:38:01.535
It's not working.

00:38:01.571 --> 00:38:03.630
I can't compensate
for the instability.

00:38:03.673 --> 00:38:06.972
There's no way to compensate
for a field that size.

00:38:11.114 --> 00:38:13.378
Captain, I'm showing
an unstable plasma manifold.

00:38:13.416 --> 00:38:14.906
We're headed for a breach.

00:38:14.951 --> 00:38:16.919
Bridge to Torres.
What's happening?

00:38:16.987 --> 00:38:20.320
We're reading
a warp core breach up here.

00:38:20.357 --> 00:38:22.018
We're on it, Captain.

00:38:22.058 --> 00:38:23.389
No time to talk.

00:38:23.426 --> 00:38:25.018
Shut down the matrix!

00:38:25.061 --> 00:38:27.029
I can't!
It's not responding!

00:38:27.063 --> 00:38:28.360
It's fused!

00:38:28.398 --> 00:38:30.832
Plasma temperature
at 43 million Kelvin!

00:38:30.867 --> 00:38:32.494
Carey, get everybody out!

00:38:32.535 --> 00:38:34.662
All right, people, let's go!
Right now!

00:38:34.704 --> 00:38:36.262
Move it out!
Move out! Come on!

00:38:36.306 --> 00:38:37.432
Let's go! Right now!

00:38:37.474 --> 00:38:39.066
Let's go, come on!
Move it out! Fast!

00:38:39.109 --> 00:38:40.076
Right now!

00:38:40.110 --> 00:38:41.941
Keep moving!

00:38:42.012 --> 00:38:43.445
I can't unlock it.

00:38:43.480 --> 00:38:46.176
The command matrix is sealed.

00:38:46.216 --> 00:38:49.913
Plasma temperature
at 50 million Kelvin!

00:38:53.556 --> 00:38:56.081
Anti-neutrino
bombardment has stopped.

00:38:56.126 --> 00:38:58.094
Plasma temperature dropping.

00:39:06.670 --> 00:39:11.733
We didn't anticipate
anti-neutrinos.

00:39:11.775 --> 00:39:14.573
The trajector could
never be compatible

00:39:14.611 --> 00:39:17.239
with Federation technology.

00:39:17.280 --> 00:39:19.578
I'll start erasing
the sensor logs.

00:39:19.616 --> 00:39:21.481
We can blame it
on the phase discrepancy.

00:39:21.518 --> 00:39:22.849
No.

00:39:22.886 --> 00:39:25.377
We're not going
to cover this up.

00:39:25.422 --> 00:39:26.411
Are you crazy?

00:39:26.456 --> 00:39:28.754
We don't have to take the blame
for this.

00:39:28.792 --> 00:39:30.623
But we're going to.

00:39:32.963 --> 00:39:35.932
We disobeyed orders,
gambling it would pay off.

00:39:35.966 --> 00:39:37.763
It didn't.

00:39:37.801 --> 00:39:40.463
And now we just can't pretend
like nothing happened.

00:39:40.503 --> 00:39:41.936
I don't understand.

00:39:41.972 --> 00:39:43.940
There's no need for this.

00:39:43.974 --> 00:39:46.602
I'm sorry
if you don't get it, Seska,

00:39:46.643 --> 00:39:49.942
but it has something
to do with, um...

00:39:49.980 --> 00:39:52.312
with being able
to live with yourself.

00:39:52.349 --> 00:39:55.785
That doesn't sound like you.

00:39:55.819 --> 00:39:57.184
You've changed.

00:39:59.189 --> 00:40:01.589
If that's true...

00:40:01.624 --> 00:40:03.956
I take it as a compliment.

00:40:10.633 --> 00:40:13.124
I take full responsibility
for what happened.

00:40:13.169 --> 00:40:16.070
There were others involved,
but I was the senior officer,

00:40:16.106 --> 00:40:19.075
and the culpability is mine.

00:40:19.109 --> 00:40:22.476
Lieutenant Torres is not
precisely correct, Captain.

00:40:22.512 --> 00:40:25.242
She was not
the senior officer involved.

00:40:25.281 --> 00:40:26.578
I was.

00:40:28.985 --> 00:40:30.452
You?

00:40:30.487 --> 00:40:33.115
It was I who made the exchange...

00:40:33.156 --> 00:40:36.319
the Federation library
for the trajector matrix.

00:40:48.371 --> 00:40:50.965
I will deal with you
in a moment.

00:40:54.310 --> 00:40:56.574
I don't have the luxury
of throwing you in the brig

00:40:56.613 --> 00:40:58.513
for the rest of this voyage.

00:40:58.548 --> 00:40:59.606
I need you.

00:40:59.649 --> 00:41:02.675
I need every person
on this ship.

00:41:04.687 --> 00:41:06.678
But I want you to know

00:41:06.723 --> 00:41:10.489
how very deeply
you have disappointed me.

00:41:12.495 --> 00:41:16.761
If there are
any further transgressions,

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:19.769
even a minor one...

00:41:19.803 --> 00:41:24.831
you will no longer be
an officer on this crew.

00:41:26.743 --> 00:41:28.108
Is that clear?

00:41:28.144 --> 00:41:30.544
Yes, ma'am.

00:41:32.749 --> 00:41:34.512
Dismissed.

00:41:42.425 --> 00:41:44.916
I don't even know
where to start.

00:41:47.197 --> 00:41:49.358
I want you to explain to me

00:41:49.399 --> 00:41:53.392
how you, of all people,
could be involved in this.

00:41:53.436 --> 00:41:55.631
It is quite simple, Captain.

00:41:55.672 --> 00:41:58.004
You have made it clear
on many occasions

00:41:58.041 --> 00:42:00.339
that your highest goal
for the crew

00:42:00.376 --> 00:42:01.775
is to get them home.

00:42:01.811 --> 00:42:03.142
But in this instance,

00:42:03.179 --> 00:42:05.443
your standards
would not allow you

00:42:05.482 --> 00:42:06.915
to violate Sikarian law.

00:42:06.950 --> 00:42:09.748
Someone had to spare you
the ethical dilemma.

00:42:09.786 --> 00:42:12.653
I was the logical choice,

00:42:12.689 --> 00:42:15.351
and so I chose to act.

00:42:19.062 --> 00:42:22.259
You did it for me...

00:42:22.298 --> 00:42:24.789
because you knew I couldn't.

00:42:25.835 --> 00:42:28.963
I accept the consequences
of my actions.

00:42:29.005 --> 00:42:30.973
I expect to lose my commission

00:42:31.007 --> 00:42:32.201
and to be court-martialed

00:42:32.242 --> 00:42:35.336
when we return
to Federation space.

00:42:47.157 --> 00:42:51.560
You are one
of my most valued officers...

00:42:51.594 --> 00:42:54.654
and you are my friend.

00:42:54.697 --> 00:42:58.394
It is vital
that you understand me here.

00:43:00.270 --> 00:43:01.999
I need you.

00:43:03.973 --> 00:43:07.704
But I also need to know
that I can count on you.

00:43:07.744 --> 00:43:10.611
You are my counsel...

00:43:10.647 --> 00:43:14.310
the one I turn to when I need
my moral compass checked.

00:43:14.350 --> 00:43:17.717
We have forged
this relationship for years,

00:43:17.754 --> 00:43:19.881
and I depend on it.

00:43:30.500 --> 00:43:32.730
I realize you made
a sacrifice for me...

00:43:32.769 --> 00:43:35.533
but it's not one

00:43:35.572 --> 00:43:39.099
I would have allowed you
to make.

00:43:39.142 --> 00:43:43.977
You can use logic
to justify almost anything.

00:43:44.047 --> 00:43:46.811
That's its power...

00:43:46.849 --> 00:43:48.316
and its flaw.

00:43:49.953 --> 00:43:51.853
From now on...

00:43:51.888 --> 00:43:55.483
bring your logic to me.

00:43:55.525 --> 00:43:58.494
Don't act on it behind my back.

00:44:00.597 --> 00:44:03.623
You have my word.

00:44:03.666 --> 00:44:07.261
My logic was not in error...

00:44:07.303 --> 00:44:09.271
but I was.

00:44:15.612 --> 00:44:17.102
Dismissed.
